---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { serviceGroups } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Services" description="Websites, applications, automation and managed digital services from Blackline Development.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
        <h1>Technology shaped around the outcome.</h1>
        <p class="hero-copy">
          We build around the actual workflow, audience and operating constraints rather than forcing every project into the same template.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="Choosing a Blackline Development service">
        <strong>Not sure what category it fits?</strong>
        <p>Describe the result you need. Discovery comes before a technical commitment.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container card-grid">
      {serviceGroups.map((service, index) => (
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">0{index + 1}</span>
          <h3>{service.title}</h3>
          <p>{service.summary}</p>
          <p class="detail">{service.detail}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">How the work moves</p>
          <h2>Understand first. Build second.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The process is designed to reduce surprises. The requirement is understood before the implementation grows around assumptions that have never been checked.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">01</span>
          <h3>Define the outcome</h3>
          <p>Start with what needs to change, who it affects and what a useful result looks like.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">02</span>
          <h3>Scope the real work</h3>
          <p>Identify dependencies, unknowns and constraints before treating an estimate as a reliable price.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">03</span>
          <h3>Build in reviewable steps</h3>
          <p>Keep changes focused and understandable so problems can be caught before they become expensive to unwind.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="card-index">04</span>
          <h3>Hando over or keep it managed</h3>
          <p>Take ownership of the finished work, or add only the hosting, maintenance and managed services you actually want.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split-panel">
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Commissioned work</p>
        <h3>Build something specific.</h3>
        <p>Scope and price the actual project first, then choose the service pace that fits.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/commissions">Commissioned development</a>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Ongoing services</p>
        <h3>Keep the infrastructure managed.</h3>
        <p>Hosting, maintenance, email and domain management remain separate subscriptions.</p>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/managed-services">Managed services</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
